# /sdd-dependencies

Purpose:
  Analyze and visualize the project dependency graph. Detects cycles,
  computes topological order, identifies critical path, and surfaces
  circular or missing dependencies.

Owns: commands/sdd-dependencies.sdd

Description:
  Reads .sdd/dependencies/graph.sdd to produce a dependency health
  report. Shows task dependency graph, cycle detection, topological
  sort, critical path, parallel capacity, and missing dependencies.
  Supports export to DOT and Mermaid formats for visualization.

Usage:
  /sdd-dependencies
  /sdd-dependencies --graph
  /sdd-dependencies --cycles
  /sdd-dependencies --critical-path
  /sdd-dependencies --topological
  /sdd-dependencies --export <format>
  /sdd-dependencies --json

Options:
  --graph          Show full dependency graph
  --cycles         Show only cyclic dependencies
  --critical-path  Show critical path and bottleneck tasks
  --topological    Show topological sort order
  --export         Export to dot or mermaid format
  --json           Output machine-readable JSON

Mode: READ_ONLY

DependencyGraph:
  nodes: tasks (T-XXX)
  edges: dependency relationships (T-A -> T-B means T-B depends on T-A)
  rules:
    - Tasks without incoming edges can run in parallel
    - Cycles MUST be flagged as errors
    - Critical path is the longest dependency chain

Output:
  DEPENDENCY GRAPH

    Total Tasks:         <count>
    Total Dependencies:  <count>
    Cycles Detected:     <count>
    Critical Path:       <length> tasks
    Parallel Capacity:   <count> tasks

  Graph:
    T100 (Domain) -----> T103 (Refund Service)
    T101 (Repository) --> T103
    T102 (Provider) ---> T103
    T103 (Refund) -----> T104 (API)
    T104 (API) --------> T106 (Review)

  Cycles:
    [CYCLE-001] T201 <-> T202 (mutual dependency)

  Critical Path:
    T100 -> T103 -> T104 -> T106 (4 tasks, estimated duration: N days)

  Topological Order:
    1. T100, T101, T102 (parallel)
    2. T103
    3. T104, T105 (parallel)
    4. T106

Rules:
  [DEP-01] /sdd-dependencies MUST NOT modify any files.
  [DEP-02] Cycle detection MUST be performed on every invocation.
  [DEP-03] Critical path MUST account for task duration estimates.
  [DEP-04] Parallel capacity MUST show tasks with no dependencies between them.
  [DEP-05] Export formats MUST be valid DOT or Mermaid syntax.
  [DEP-06] Missing dependencies MUST be flagged as warnings.

Navigation:
   INDEX: @INDEX.sdd
   DependenciesIndex: @../dependencies/INDEX.sdd
   DependenciesGraph: @../dependencies/graph.sdd
   DependenciesLocking: @../dependencies/locking.sdd
